    "Description": "### Impact\nAn M4A file containing a sub-atom with a size of zero in the `----` atom makes the parser enter an infinite loop, resulting in a denial-of-service for programs reading such files with tinytag.\n\n### Patches\nThe issue has been fixed in tinytag 2.3.0, by reusing the primary atom parsing code path that contains appropriate size checks.\n\n### Workarounds\nNo workarounds exist. Users must upgrade to tinytag 2.3.0.",
